is preferred that the three additional upper-division courses for the plan are selected from:"}],"label":"Plan","notes":"The remainder of the course of study consists of a plan, to be worked out by students in consultation with their designated departmental adviser, that details which courses they take to complete the degree. The plan must be worked out five terms before the student expects to graduate. There must be one course in the Physics 170 series and one course in the Physics 180 series, or two courses in the Physics 180 series. There must be three additional upper-division courses in the plan. There must be written rationale for the plan. Except for the Physics 180 laboratories, the courses need not be in the Physics and Astronomy Department. However, it is expected that the courses fit into a coherent structure. It is important that the structure and rationale are thought out carefully, as the plan must be endorsed by the designated adviser and be approved by the departmental academic affairs committee. Pre-approved plans of study are available from the undergraduate advisers."},{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 108","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 114","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS M122","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 123","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 124","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 126","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 132","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 140A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 140B","status":"inactive"}],"label":"Preparation for Graduate School","notes":"Students preparing for graduate school should take additional courses in physics and mathematics. Recommended courses are:"}],"label":"The Major"}},{"name":"Honors Program","requirement":{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 199","status":"inactive"}],"label":"Research-Based","notes":"Students must complete two 4-unit terms of Physics 199."},{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 197","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 115A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"choose","items":[{"type":"course","code":"MATH 120A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"MATH 120B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 221A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 221B","status":"inactive"}],"count":2,"label":"Elective","notes":"Select two courses from:"}],"label":"Course-Based","notes":"Students must take 4 units of Physics 197—an in-depth individual study of a physics topic of interest to the student under the guidance of a faculty member and resulting in a written report—and are also required to take Mathematics 115A and two courses selected from Mathematics 120A, 120B, Physics 221A, or 221B."}],"label":"Honors Program","notes":"In addition to completing all courses required for the major, students must complete one of the two honors program options."}},{"name":"Preparation for the Major","requirement":{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 1A","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 1B","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 1C","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 4AL","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 4BL","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 17","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 32","status":"inactive"},{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 1AH","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 1BH","status":"inactive"},{"type":"course","code":"PHYSICS 1CH","status":"inactive"}],"label":"Physics 1 Honors series","notes":"Students may substitute courses from the Physics 1 honors series for the Physics 1 series."}],"label":"Physics"},{"type":"all","items":[{"type":"course","code":"CHEM 20A","statu